From 0162e4124dae18af0cde79b9136907f208ebf318 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nomorecoolnicknames <78512247+nomorecoolnicknames@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 14:12:17 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: pmi8994_fg: read charger status live

The fuel gauge answers POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_STATUS from a cached
chip->status that is only refreshed by the charger's
power_supply_changed notifications. When the charger never emits such
an event after probe, the cache stays POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_UNKNOWN and
the property falls back to the capacity/current-based estimate, which
reports Discharging even while a charger is plugged in. Observed on
the Meizu M6 Note (m1721, PMI8950).

Query the charger's status property directly instead of relying on the
cached value, and keep the current-based fallback for when the charger
is absent or the read fails.

Signed-off-by: nomorecoolnicknames <78512247+nomorecoolnicknames@users.noreply.github.com>
Assisted-by: Claude (Anthropic)
---
 drivers/power/supply/pmi8994_fg.c | 14 +++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/pmi8994_fg.c b/drivers/power/supply/pmi8994_fg.c
index eafa8fd97..e9cb7a5b8 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/pmi8994_fg.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/pmi8994_fg.c
@@ -624,9 +624,17 @@ static int pmi8994_fg_get_property(struct power_supply *psy,
 
 	switch (psp) {
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_STATUS:
-		/* Get status from charger if available */
-		if (chip->chg_psy && chip->status != POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_UNKNOWN) {
-			val->intval = chip->status;
+		/*
+		 * Get status from the charger if available. Read it live: the
+		 * cached chip->status can stay UNKNOWN when the charger never
+		 * emits a power_supply_changed event after probe, which makes
+		 * the current-based fallback report Discharging even while a
+		 * charger is plugged in.
+		 */
+		if (chip->chg_psy &&
+		    !power_supply_get_property(chip->chg_psy,
+					      POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_STATUS, val)) {
+			/* val->intval already set from the charger */
 		} else {
 			/*
 			 * Fall back to capacity and current-based
